{
  "id": "COMPOUND:737 - DISEASE:1932",
  "verbalization": "Isoflurane, through its interaction with the coiled-coil domain containing 33, appears to influence the development of Macrostomia. This relationship is supported by multiple pathways, all of which indicate a causal link between isoflurane and the condition associated with Macrostomia. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust biological mechanism, where isoflurane modulates the coiled-coil domain containing 33, which in turn affects the progression or manifestation of Macrostomia. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for the coiled-coil domain containing 33 in the pathophysiology of Macrostomia, possibly through regulatory or structural interactions. The evidence points to a mechanism involving molecular signaling or cellular regulation, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
